---
/**
 * Retainer — the section Two ways in opens onto.
 *
 * A PLACEHOLDER. Its copy and its layout are still to be given; what is here
 * is a ground and a holding line, so the mechanism above it can be built and
 * seen working before the content exists. Replace the body of this file and
 * nothing else has to change: Two ways in renders it inside a clip that is
 * already the size of the screen, so whatever goes in here is drawn at its
 * final size from the first frame and never scales.
 *
 * Deliberately NOT a <section> of its own in the page's flow. It is only ever
 * seen through the window in Two ways in, and a second copy of it below would
 * be the same chapter twice. When its content lands, the question of whether
 * it also wants a life of its own further down the page is worth asking then.
 *
 * It does NOT carry `data-nav-over="dark"`, even though its ground is dark and
 * every other dark stretch of the page declares itself that way. The nav reads
 * a zone's bounding box, and this element's box is the whole screen from the
 * first frame — a clip changes what is painted, not what is measured — so the
 * capsule would turn to glass over Two ways in's cream while the window was
 * still a rectangle at the foot of the page. The declaration is on
 * `[data-two-zone]` in TwoWays.astro instead, which is sized to the window
 * itself and grows with it.
 */
---

<div class="retainer" data-retainer>
  <p class="retainer__holding">Retainer</p>
</div>

<style>
  .retainer {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    /* The reference's flat grey. It is a placeholder colour, not a token: when
       the real ground arrives it will be this section's own, and inventing a
       --color-bg-retainer for a stand-in would put a name in globals.css that
       has to be changed rather than filled. */
    background: #b3b3b3;
  }

  .retainer__holding {
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.35);
  }
</style>
